WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome to our video, "Register a Trademark for Your Brand."

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
At Amazon, we encourage brands to trademark their brand names and logos.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
That means legally registering them with a designated government office in a specific country.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.565
By registering a brand name or logo, a brand receives verification from that office that they're

00:00:19.565 --> 00:00:22.000
the owner of products identified by it.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
That gives them legal rights and protections for their brand name or logo,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
which is considered intellectual property or IP in a country where it is trademarked.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.261
Trademarking is also one of two basic requirements brands meet in order to enroll in and enjoy the

00:00:38.261 --> 00:00:40.000
benefits of Amazon Brand Registry.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.333
The other is a brand name or a logo that includes a brand name permanently affixed to their products

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:47.000
or packaging.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.000
If a brand doesn't want to trademark their brand name or logo,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.000
they can submit a request to Amazon to list their products using an unregistered brand name.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.000
They may also be able to sell products generically in the Amazon store,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.688
but we recommend trademarking whenever possible because of the legal protections and additional

00:01:05.688 --> 00:01:07.000
benefits it provides.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.176
It's worth getting familiar with the trademarking process and the resources Amazon offers to help

00:01:13.176 --> 00:01:14.000
complete it,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
even if you aren't yet ready to pursue a trademark.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:23.000
To enroll in Brand Registry, you need an active registered trademark for your brand name or logo,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:30.000
or in some cases you can enroll using a pending trademark application or a pending trademark registration.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.000
If you want to use a registered trademark to enroll in Brand Registry,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.684
it needs to be issued by the designated government office of a country where Amazon has a corresponding

00:01:39.684 --> 00:01:40.000
store.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.000
As a reminder, here's the full list.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.043
In the US, for example, trademarks for brand names and logos are issued by the United States Patent

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:52.000
and Trademark Office, or USPTO.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.222
Brands prove they own the rights to their trademark by submitting a trademark number during Brand

00:01:58.222 --> 00:01:59.000
Registry enrollment.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.000
That number appears on the trademark certificate they receive from the designated government office.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.000
If you want to use a pending trademark application to enroll in Brand Registry,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.950
it also needs to be secured from the designated government office of a country where Amazon has

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.000
a corresponding store.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.000
You can get assistance securing a pending application through Amazon's IP Accelerator program.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.000
To learn more about that program, watch our Seller University video,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.000
register a trademark through IP Accelerator,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.000
or get started by visiting brandservices.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:32.500
amazon.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.000
com,

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.000
hovering over tools, and clicking IP Accelerator.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.000
If you want to use a pending trademark registration to enroll in Brand Registry,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.000
you need to secure it from one of the offices Amazon accepts pending registrations from.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:52.000
To check whether your pending registration can be used for brand registry enrollment,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.000
search Seller Central for enrollment guidelines for accepted trademark offices.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Click the link for the relevant trademark office,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.000
then look for information about pending registrations and trademark statuses.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:11.562
It's important to note that all trademarks, whether active or pending, are registered with individual

00:03:11.562 --> 00:03:12.000
countries.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.000
You're only required to have a trademark in one country when you want to enroll with Amazon.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:21.000
After a single country's trademark has been approved by Brand Registry,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.000
you'll have a global account that can be used for every Amazon store worldwide.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.000
But if you plan to have your product sold in multiple countries, across multiple Amazon stores,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:36.000
we recommend submitting a trademark to Brand Registry for each country.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.000
That's because, while Amazon extends the privileges of brand enrollment across all our stores,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.000
the IP rights and legal protections of a government verified trademark remain country specific.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.696
For example, let's say you want to enroll in Brand Registry so that your products can be listed

00:03:52.696 --> 00:03:54.000
as part of your brand.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
When they're sold in our US and India stores.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:03.000
In that case, you'd only be required to secure one trademark, either from the USPTO,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:09.000
or the Office of the Controller General of Patents, Designs and Trademarks in India.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:15.800
You could use that one trademark to enroll in Brand Registry and enjoy related benefits while selling

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.000
in both countries.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.727
But to ensure that your brand and products receive the same IP rights and legal protections in both

00:04:22.727 --> 00:04:24.000
the US and India,

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:30.533
we'd recommend registering a trademark in both countries and submitting both trademarks to Brand

00:04:30.533 --> 00:04:31.000
Registry.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.000
You'd submit the first trademark for approval during enrollment.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.000
After that first trademark is approved and your brand is enrolled with Amazon,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:44.333
you'd then use the Manage Intellectual Properties Tool in the Brand Registry Portal to connect the

00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:46.000
second trademark to your brand.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.600
The trademarks you obtain from one or more countries government offices must be text-based word

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.000
marks for brand names,

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.000
or image-based design marks for logos.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:01.517
If you decide to trademark a logo, keep in mind that any image-based design mark you want to use

00:05:01.517 --> 00:05:04.000
in the Amazon store must include your brand name.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.000
This requirement allows us to confirm that brands are paired with the correct products.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:14.923
To obtain either type of trademark, start by going to brandservices.

00:05:14.923 --> 00:05:15.462
amazon.

00:05:15.462 --> 00:05:16.000
com.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:21.667
Click the Get Started With Brand Registry button, then click the Get Started button on the next

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:22.000
page.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.000
Scroll down and click You Can Review Country Specific Requirements here.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Then select the country where you want to register and review the list of requirements.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.500
Click the link to the Relevant Trademark Office's website.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:39.000
That's where you can begin the official registration process

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:44.333
and obtain the trademark you'll need to enroll in Brand Registry, or the Pending Trademark Application

00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:45.000
or Registration.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:51.909
If you plan to trademark your brand name or logo with the USPTO, note that it has both principal

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:53.000
and supplemental registers.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:58.143
Your brand assets must go on their principal register if you want to use your trademark to enroll

00:05:58.143 --> 00:05:59.000
in Brand Registry.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.895
The principal register is primary, offers the greatest level of protection for trademark owners,

00:06:04.895 --> 00:06:07.000
and offers brands recognition worldwide.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:12.850
While some product owners complete the trademark registration process themselves using guides or

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.000
educational materials provided by the registering office,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.000
we encourage brands to seek assistance from a trademark attorney or law firm.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.000
If you don't already have a preferred partner for the trademark registration process,

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.000
we encourage you to take advantage of the Amazon IP Accelerator Program,

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.833
which can help connect you with trusted IP law firms that provide trademark registration services

00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:37.000
at competitive rates.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:42.000
After you have the required trademark, you're ready to enroll your brand with Amazon.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:48.588
For step-by-step instructions, see our Seller University video Enroll Your Brand in Amazon Brand

00:06:48.588 --> 00:06:49.000
Registry.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:53.000
This concludes our video on registering a trademark for your brand.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:56.400
Thank you, and happy selling in the Amazon Store!
